<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2013/05/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>VL.Mapsui</id>
    <!-- The WORKING version: always one ahead of what is on nuget.org (0.0.4-alpha, 2026-11-15), so a
         local repack can never be mistaken for the published package in a NuGet cache. Managed in
         step with VL.NetTopologySuite; the dependency below is the oldest PUBLISHED version of it
         that this package's help works with (0.0.8-alpha: SetSRID, which the help uses since 2026-11-15; FromWKT came in 0.0.6), never its working version. -->
    <version>0.0.5-alpha</version>
    <title>VL.Mapsui — Mapsui map engine nodes for vvvv gamma</title>
    <authors>red</authors>
    <owners>red</owners>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/rednotfound/VL.Mapsui</projectUrl>
    <!-- nuget.org shows this on the package page. The path is the path INSIDE the package (README.md
         is packed to docs\ below), and nuget pack refuses to pack if it is not in <files>. Settled
         the same way in VL.NetTopologySuite, 2026-09-25. -->
    <readme>docs\README.md</readme>
    <description>Maps in VL, built on Mapsui: OpenStreetMap or any tile service, with your own geometry and features on top.</description>
    <summary>Maps in VL, built on Mapsui: OpenStreetMap or any tile service, with your own geometry and features on top.</summary>
    <releaseNotes>
      0.0.5-alpha (2026-11-18) - No node changed. With this package installed,
      VL.NetTopologySuite's GeometryEditor window draws OpenStreetMap under the drawing when the
      editor's SRID is 4326 or 3857 (the B key switches it). The tiles are the OpenStreetMap
      layer's own, from the same disk cache, so a place already seen on a map is there in the
      editor; at most two are downloaded at a time and none off screen. Requires
      VL.NetTopologySuite 0.0.10-alpha.

      0.0.4-alpha (2026-11-15) - Geometry and FeatureLayer read each geometry's
      SRID: 0 and 4326 are longitude and latitude as before, 3857 is drawn as it is, and any other
      is not drawn - Status names the code and says to Reproject (VL.PROJ) to 4326 first. Geometry
      has a new Status output. What Pick hands back is labelled SRID 4326. OpenStreetMap and XYZ now
      fetch as soon as they are drawn: Enabled is on by default (switch it off, or keep the toggle,
      for a patch that must open offline). The mouse moves the map without any wiring - left drag
      pans, the wheel zooms. ToSkiaLayer's new Interactive pin
      switches that off, and a Drag, ZoomByWheel or Click node wired to the map takes that gesture
      over, so patches made with 0.0.2-alpha behave as before - except a map that was meant to
      stand still, which now needs Interactive off. The map presses its own widgets: ZoomButtons
      work without a Click node. UI drawn over the map in a Group needs one wire, IsAnyItemHovered
      to NOT to Interactive (HowTo Put UI over the map). New help patch: HowTo Draw
      geometry in another CRS. New node MapWindow: a map
      in one node, with its window (help: HowTo Open a map window, HowTo Put UI over the map; 33 nodes, 22 patches). Requires VL.NetTopologySuite 0.0.8-alpha, for SetSRID.

      0.0.3-alpha (2026-11-15) - No node added, removed or changed; 32 nodes. Fixed: GeometryLayer and
      FeatureLayer skip an empty geometry as they skip a missing one. Since VL.NetTopologySuite
      0.0.8-alpha a node whose input is missing gives an empty geometry instead of nothing, and one
      empty geometry stretched the layer's extent from your data to the map's origin, off the coast of
      Africa. The README is the short one the vvvv libraries have; the long read is docs/GUIDE.md on
      GitHub.

      0.0.2-alpha (2026-11-08) - No node added, removed or changed; 32 nodes. Every node's tooltip
      is now short: a one-line summary, a sentence of usage and a line per pin. The help follows
      VL.NetTopologySuite 0.0.6-alpha, which renamed Read WKT and Write WKT to FromWKT and ToWKT,
      and this version requires it: a patch of yours made with the older VL.NetTopologySuite shows
      Read WKT unresolved - put FromWKT in its place.

      0.0.1-alpha (2026-09-26) - The first release, a prerelease. 32 nodes in eight categories - Mapsui,
      Mapsui.Layers, Mapsui.Styles, Mapsui.Navigate, Mapsui.Project, Mapsui.Widgets, Mapsui.Skia,
      Mapsui.Debug - 244 tests, 19 help patches, and F1 on every node opens one. Tile layers
      (OpenStreetMap, any XYZ service) with a shared disk cache, geometry and feature layers, a
      graticule, five styles, navigation, picking, pixel/degree conversion and widgets. Wraps
      Mapsui 4.1.9; verified in vvvv gamma 7.4. Fetching is off until you switch it on. Not ready
      for real work: the node surface may still change between prereleases.
    </releaseNotes>
    <copyright>Copyright 2026 VL.Mapsui Contributors</copyright>
    <!-- The "VL" tag is what makes the pack discoverable at https://vvvv.org/packs -->
    <tags>VL vvvv gamma map mapsui gis openstreetmap tiles skia</tags>
    <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/rednotfound/VL.Mapsui" />

    <!--
      These must match the NugetDependency lines in VL.Mapsui.vl. The .vl is what teaches VL
      the types, so a node whose signature mentions Mapsui.Map only exists because Mapsui is
      declared there; the nuspec is what makes the package resolvable for a consumer.

      VL.Core, VL.Core.Skia, VL.CoreLib, VL.Skia and SkiaSharp are deliberately absent: they
      ship inside vvvv, which substitutes its own copies for anything declared here.
    -->
    <dependencies>
      <group targetFramework="net8.0">
        <dependency id="Mapsui"                version="4.1.9" />
        <dependency id="Mapsui.Tiling"         version="4.1.9" />
        <dependency id="NetTopologySuite"      version="2.6.0" />
        <dependency id="NetTopologySuite.Features" version="2.1.0" />
        <!--
          The package that MAKES geometry, which this one only draws. Declared so that installing
          VL.Mapsui brings it along and the help patch that draws a shape opens working: vvvv does
          not fetch a missing document dependency by itself - it shows the entry red and offers to
          install on rightclick.

          vvvv's own packs get away without this (VL.Skia's help uses VL.ImGui, VL.Audio declares no
          VL dependency at all and its help uses VL.Stride) because everything there ships inside
          vvvv and is therefore always present. Nothing guarantees that for us.
        -->
        <dependency id="VL.NetTopologySuite"   version="0.0.10-alpha" />
        <dependency id="Mapsui.Rendering.Skia" version="4.1.9" />
      </group>
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <files>
    <!-- Entry point. Must sit at the package root, no subfolder. -->
    <file src="VL.Mapsui.vl" target="" />

    <file src="src\VL.Mapsui\bin\Release\net8.0\VL.Mapsui.dll" target="lib\net8.0\" />
    <file src="src\VL.Mapsui\bin\Release\net8.0\VL.Mapsui.xml" target="lib\net8.0\" />

    <!-- This package's own examples. target stays help\ because that is where vvvv looks. -->
    <file src="help\VL.Mapsui\**\*.vl" target="help\" />

    <!--
      Help.xml orders the help patches in the browser and carries their search tags. It needs its
      own line: the glob above takes .vl and nothing else, so leaving this out would ship the
      patches unordered and untagged with no warning anywhere.
    -->
    <file src="help\VL.Mapsui\Help.xml" target="help\" />

    <!--
      README.md is also the nuget.org page (<readme> above). NOTES.md is deliberately NOT shipped:
      it is a 2000-line working log of this repository, full of machine paths, and a user reading
      the package wants the design, not the forensics.
    -->
    <file src="LICENSE" target="docs\LICENSE" />
    <file src="README.md" target="docs\" />
    <file src="docs\ARCHITECTURE.md" target="docs\" />
    <file src="docs\MAPSUI-SURFACE.md" target="docs\" />
  </files>
</package>
